162	\begin{lemma}[van Kampen]
163	\label{lemma:van-kampen}
164		Suppose $\m P$ is a valid $G$-picture with boundary word $w$. Let $J^a$ be the product of the labels of the vertices in $\m P$. Then $w=J^a$ is a valid relation in $G$. Moreover, we say that the relation $w=J^a$ is \emph{witnessed} by the $G$-picture $\m P$.
165	\end{lemma}
166	The proof is elementary and relies on the fact that the subgroup $\braket J$ is abelian and central, so that cyclic permutations of relations are valid relations.  
167	By counting what goes on at each step in the induction of a proof of the above lemma, one can extract a quantitative version. This is stated and proved in \S \ref{subsection:quant-van-kampen}. 
