169	\begin{prop}
170	\label{prop: perfect strategy}
171		Let $\s: \G \to U(\C^D)$ be an operator solution. Define a strategy by setting $\ket\psi = \ket{\r{EPR}_D}$, $A_e^{(v)} = \s(e)$ for all $e,v,$ and $B_e = \bar{\s(e)}$ for all $e$. Provers using this strategy win with probability $1$.
